      "page": 4,
      "marks": 5,
      "syllabus_outcomes": ["1.1"],
      "topic": "Quadratics - Discriminant for intersection",
      "answers": {
        "answer_snippet": "x² + 2cx + 4 = 4x + c leading to x² + 2cx - 4x + 4 - c = 0. Discriminant: b² - 4ac = (2c - 4)² - 4(4 - c) = 4c² - 12c. For two distinct points: 4c(c - 3) > 0. Answer: c < 0, c > 3"
      }
    },
